{"id":10470,"date":"2026-05-13T11:47:26","date_gmt":"2026-05-13T11:47:26","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/?p=10470"},"modified":"2026-05-13T11:47:26","modified_gmt":"2026-05-13T11:47:26","slug":"7-warning-signs-you-need-termite-control-in-your-melbourne-home","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/7-warning-signs-you-need-termite-control-in-your-melbourne-home\/","title":{"rendered":"7 Warning Signs You Need Termite Control in Your Melbourne Home"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Most homeowners don&#8217;t think about termites \u2014 until it&#8217;s too late.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">By the time you actually see damage, termites may have already been quietly eating through your walls, floors, or roof for months. Sometimes years.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">That&#8217;s the scary part. These little insects don&#8217;t make a big scene. They just get to work, hidden behind your plaster, under your floorboards, or deep inside your timber frames.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you live in Melbourne, the risk is real. Our warm summers and sometimes damp conditions are exactly what termite colonies love. And with so many older homes around the city, there&#8217;s no shortage of timber for them to feed on.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The good news? If you catch the signs early, professional <\/span><b>termite control in Melbourne<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> can stop the damage before it gets out of hand.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Here are 7 warning signs you should never ignore.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2><b>1. Your Timber Sounds Hollow When You Knock on It<\/b><\/h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Go ahead \u2014 tap on your skirting boards, door frames, or wooden walls. Does it sound solid? Or does it sound a bit&#8230; empty?<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Termites eat wood from the inside out. So the surface might look perfectly fine while there&#8217;s nothing left underneath. That hollow sound is one of the earliest signs homeowners notice \u2014 and one of the most telling.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Try tapping along different sections. If certain spots sound hollow and others don&#8217;t, that&#8217;s worth investigating. Don&#8217;t ignore it.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2><b>2. You Can See Mud Tubes Along Your Walls or Foundation<\/b><\/h2>\n<p><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone  wp-image-10475\" src=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.37-AM-300x200.jpeg\" alt=\"Termite Control Melbourne:\" width=\"720\" height=\"480\" srcset=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.37-AM-300x200.jpeg 300w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.37-AM-1024x682.jpeg 1024w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.37-AM-768x512.jpeg 768w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.37-AM-1536x1023.jpeg 1536w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.37-AM.jpeg 1600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Mud tubes look like small dirt tunnels running along your walls, slab edge, or even up through your subfloor area. They&#8217;re usually about the width of a pencil.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Termites build these to travel safely between their nest and their food source \u2014 your home. The tubes protect them from open air and keep moisture in.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you spot these around your home&#8217;s exterior, inside your garage, under the house, or along fence posts \u2014 take it seriously. That&#8217;s a sign of an active colony nearby.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can break a section of the tube open. If termites appear or if it gets repaired within a day or two, you&#8217;ve got live activity. Time to call in a <\/span><b>termite pest control<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> professional straight away.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2><b>3. Wings Left Behind Near Windows or Doors<\/b><\/h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Every spring and summer in Melbourne, termite swarms happen. Winged termites leave their colony, fly out to find a mate, and start a new nest somewhere nearby \u2014 possibly inside your home.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">After they land, they drop their wings. So if you find small, translucent wings piled up near a windowsill, door frame, or light fitting \u2014 that&#8217;s a red flag.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">These wings are often mistaken for flying ant wings. But termite wings are all roughly the same size, while flying ant wings are different lengths. Either way, either insect in your home is a problem.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The swarming season in Melbourne usually runs from October through to February. Keep an eye out during these months.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2><b>4. Your Doors or Windows Are Suddenly Hard to Open<\/b><\/h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You&#8217;ve had no issues with that door for years. Now it&#8217;s stiff, sticking, or just won&#8217;t open smoothly. It&#8217;s easy to blame the weather \u2014 and sometimes that&#8217;s the cause \u2014 but termites could be the real culprit.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">When termites work through timber frames, they produce moisture as a by-product. That moisture causes the wood to swell and warp. The result? Doors and windows that no longer fit their frames properly.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Don&#8217;t just plane the door and move on. Check the surrounding timber carefully. Press on it with your thumb. If it feels soft, spongy, or easily dented \u2014 you&#8217;ve likely got a termite problem.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><b>5. Paint That&#8217;s Bubbling, Peeling, or Looks Like It Has Water Behind It<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Bubbling or blistering paint doesn&#8217;t always mean a leaking pipe. Sometimes, it means termites.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As they chew through timber and move around inside your walls, they create moisture. That moisture pushes up against your paint, causing it to bubble or peel even when there&#8217;s no obvious water source nearby.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This sign is easy to miss because it looks so much like general water damage. But if you&#8217;re seeing this in areas without any known plumbing or roof leaks \u2014 especially along timber-framed walls \u2014 book a <\/span><b>termite inspection in Melbourne<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to be sure.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><b>6. Tiny Droppings Near Timber Areas (Called Frass)<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Termite droppings are small, pellet-shaped, and usually the same colour as the wood nearby. They tend to look like sawdust or coffee grounds piled up near skirting boards, windowsills, or wooden furniture.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is called frass, and it&#8217;s a sure sign of drywood termites feeding inside the timber. These termites push their droppings out of small holes as they tunnel through the wood.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you&#8217;re regularly sweeping up what looks like fine wood dust from the same spot and there&#8217;s no obvious explanation \u2014 look closer. It might not be dust at all.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><b>7. A Faint Clicking or Rustling Sound Inside Your Walls<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone  wp-image-10475\" src=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.37-AM-300x200.jpeg\" alt=\"Termite Control Melbourne:\" width=\"653\" height=\"435\" srcset=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.37-AM-300x200.jpeg 300w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.37-AM-1024x682.jpeg 1024w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.37-AM-768x512.jpeg 768w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.37-AM-1536x1023.jpeg 1536w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.37-AM.jpeg 1600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 653px) 100vw, 653px\" \/><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This one surprises most people. Termites can actually be heard \u2014 if you know what to listen for.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Soldier termites bang their heads against the timber to signal danger to the rest of the colony. Worker termites chewing through wood also create a faint rustling or tapping sound. It&#8217;s subtle, but in a quiet room \u2014 especially at night \u2014 some homeowners have noticed it.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you press your ear to a wall and hear a soft clicking or papery rustling from inside, that&#8217;s worth getting checked out. Don&#8217;t dismiss it as the house settling.<\/span><\/p>\n<h4><b>What Should You Do If You Notice Any of These Signs?<\/b><\/h4>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone  wp-image-10476\" src=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.36-AM-300x158.jpeg\" alt=\"Termite Control Melbourne:\" width=\"835\" height=\"440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.36-AM-300x158.jpeg 300w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.36-AM-1024x540.jpeg 1024w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.36-AM-768x405.jpeg 768w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.36-AM-1536x809.jpeg 1536w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-05-11-at-10.29.36-AM.jpeg 1600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 835px) 100vw, 835px\" \/><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">First \u2014 don&#8217;t panic, but don&#8217;t wait either.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The worst thing you can do is start poking around, pulling up boards, or trying DIY treatments from the hardware store. Disturbing an active colony can cause them to scatter and relocate deeper into your home, making the problem harder \u2014 and more expensive \u2014 to fix.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Here&#8217;s what to do instead:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Note where you spotted the sign<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> \u2014 walls, subfloor, garden beds, etc.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Take a few photos<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> if possible<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Call a licensed pest control professional<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> as soon as you can<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A trained technician will carry out a full <\/span><b>termite inspection in Melbourne<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, identify the species, locate the colony, and recommend the right treatment \u2014 whether that&#8217;s a chemical barrier, a baiting system, or something else suited to your property.<\/span><\/p>\n<h4><b>Don&#8217;t Wait Until the Damage is Done<\/b><\/h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Termites don&#8217;t take days off. While you&#8217;re going about your normal life, they&#8217;re working 24 hours a day. And the longer they&#8217;re left unchecked, the more costly the repairs become.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The signs above are your early warning system. The moment you spot even one of them, it&#8217;s time to act.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/\"><b>7 States Pest Control<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, we specialise in <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/termite-pest-control\/\"><b>termite control in Melbourne<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> for homeowners who want fast, reliable answers \u2014 not guesswork. Our team knows Melbourne&#8217;s local conditions, the termite species most common in the area, and how to protect your home properly.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Whether you need a routine inspection or urgent treatment, we&#8217;re here to help.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/contact-us\/\"><b>Book <\/b><\/a><b>your termite inspection today<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> \u2014 before a small problem becomes a big one.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For trusted<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/\"> <b>pest control Melbourne<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> services, we deliver complete pest solutions. Our offerings include<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/spider-control-treatment-melbourne\/\"> <b>spider control services<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and expert<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/spider-control-treatment-melbourne\/\"> <b>spider removal service<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. We also cover<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/fox-pest-control-in-melbourne\/\"> <b>fox population control<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/possum-pest-control\/\"> <b>possum removal service Melbourne<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Ensure complete protection with our<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/termite-pest-control\/\"> <b>termite control Melbourne<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and long-lasting<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/termite-pest-control\/\"> <b>termite treatment Melbourne<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.<\/span><\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Most homeowners don&#8217;t think about termites \u2014 until it&#8217;s too late. By the time you actually see damage, termites may have already been quietly eating through your walls, floors, or roof for months. Sometimes years. That&#8217;s the scary part. These little insects don&#8217;t make a big scene. They just get to work, hidden behind your [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":10473,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[23],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-10470","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-affordable-pest-control-melbourne"],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v25.4 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/wordpress\/plugins\/seo\/ -->\n<title>Termite Control Melbourne: 7 Warning Signs<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Worried about termites? Here are 7 clear warning signs Melbourne homeowners should never ignore when to call a professional\" \/>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/7-warning-signs-you-need-termite-control-in-your-melbourne-home\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Termite Control Melbourne: 7 Warning Signs\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Worried about termites? Here are 7 clear warning signs Melbourne homeowners should never ignore when to call a professional\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/7-warning-signs-you-need-termite-control-in-your-melbourne-home\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"7 States Pest Control\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2026-05-13T11:47:26+00:00\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/7-states-4.png\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1200\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"630\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image\/png\" \/>\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"7 States Pest Control\" \/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" \/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"7 States Pest Control\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"7 minutes\" \/>\n<script type=\"application\/ld+json\" class=\"yoast-schema-graph\">{\"@context\":\"https:\/\/schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@type\":\"Article\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/7-warning-signs-you-need-termite-control-in-your-melbourne-home\/#article\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/7-warning-signs-you-need-termite-control-in-your-melbourne-home\/\"},\"author\":{\"name\":\"7 States Pest Control\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/#\/schema\/person\/d2eebd8e6e8b6f07170a10bc11d3dadb\"},\"headline\":\"7 Warning Signs You Need Termite Control in Your Melbourne Home\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-05-13T11:47:26+00:00\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/7-warning-signs-you-need-termite-control-in-your-melbourne-home\/\"},\"wordCount\":1245,\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/#organization\"},\"image\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/7-warning-signs-you-need-termite-control-in-your-melbourne-home\/#primaryimage\"},\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/7-states-4.png\",\"articleSection\":[\"Affordable Pest Control Melbourne\"],\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/7-warning-signs-you-need-termite-control-in-your-melbourne-home\/\",\"url\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/7-warning-signs-you-need-termite-control-in-your-melbourne-home\/\",\"name\":\"Termite Control Melbourne: 7 Warning Signs\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/#website\"},\"primaryImageOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/7-warning-signs-you-need-termite-control-in-your-melbourne-home\/#primaryimage\"},\"image\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/7-warning-signs-you-need-termite-control-in-your-melbourne-home\/#primaryimage\"},\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/7-states-4.png\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-05-13T11:47:26+00:00\",\"description\":\"Worried about termites? Here are 7 clear warning signs Melbourne homeowners should never ignore when to call a professional\",\"breadcrumb\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/7-warning-signs-you-need-termite-control-